{"number": 50, "text": "          Exercises\n\n          Put one of the letters y, i, u or win each gap to make a word. The word must contain the sound\n          or /au/. Write   or /au/ after each word.\n\n\n                                               A POLE\n          QZ\n          3B FON\n\n  20.2    Listen to this text. Find words from it which have an or /au/ sound and write them in the\n          correct part of the table.\n\n                                                             |     (4 words)        /au/ (6 words)\n            I enjoy living down town. Well, it’s very\n            noisy, of course. The traffic is loud, and the\n\n            young people  often shout when they come\n            out of the clubs. But there are lots of good\n            points too. There’s a big choice of shops,\n            and it’s easy to get around.\n\n           Follow up: Listen again and repeat, sentence by sentence.\n\n          Find a way from Start to Finish. You may pass a square only if the word in it has the sound /au/.\n          You can move  horizontally (<>) or vertically ({) only.\n              START\n\n               house           sound           group           about           mouth\n                  —+—\n                                                                                                cow)\n\n               soup                            brown           mouse           bought          south\n\n               could          couple           qrow                            would            cloud\n\n               know            Snow            touch           ought            down           count\n                                                             —                   _\n                               should           slow            blow           pound           young\n                                                    +                                         —\n               Soul           country                          +hrow                           round\n                                                                                                 y\n                                                                                                FINISH\n 20.4           and circle the words you hear.\n          1 Tie or toy?  He got a tie / toy for his birthday.\n         2  Goodbye  or Good   boy?   ‘Goodbye!’ / ‘Good  boy!’ she said.\n         3  Phoned  or found?   She phoned  / found a friend.\n         4  Tone or town?   What   an ugly tone / town!\n           Follow up: Record yourself saying the sentences in 20.4, choosing one of\n           the two words. Make a note of which words you say. Then listen to your\n           recording in about two weeks. Is it clear which words you said?\n\n\n                                                                                    | Now go to Unit 408\n\n\n                                                                      English Pronunciation in Use     49", "char_count": 2942, "mean_conf": 81.57, "word_count": 343, "words": [{"text": "Exercises", "x0": 203, "y0": 44, "x1": 528, "y1": 110, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"text": "20.1", "x0": 35, "y0": 182, "x1": 130, "y1": 222, "conf": 31, "bold": false}, {"text": "Put", "x0": 197, "y0": 189, "x1": 256, "y1": 222, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "one", "x0": 272, "y0": 198, "x1": 337, "y1": 222, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "of", "x0": 353, "y0": 189, "x1": 392, "y1": 222, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "the", "x0": 404, "y0": 189, "x1": 462, "y1": 222, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "letters", "x0": 480, "y0": 190, "x1": 593, "y1": 223, "conf": 92, "bold": false}, {"text": "y,", "x0": 610, "y0": 200, "x1": 634, "y1": 231, "conf": 92, "bold": false}, {"text": "i,", "x0": 652, "y0": 190, "x1": 667, "y1": 228, "conf": 78, "bold": false}, {"text": "u", "x0": 698, "y0": 200, "x1": 707, "y1": 223, "conf": 76, "bold": false}, {"text": "or", "x0": 7